# agentic-nix memory

## Project
Hybrid code search RAG stack: ParadeDB (pg_search BM25 + pgvector) + Ollama + MCP server.
Path: /home/sam/home/agentic-nix

## Flake structure (flake-parts, hayate/pure-ledger style)
- `flake/lib.nix` — recursiveImports helper
- `perSystem/formatter.nix` — alejandra
- `perSystem/devShells.nix` — dev shell (fenix Rust + onnxruntime + postgresql_17 + ollama + uv + just)
- `perSystem/packages.nix` — crane build for `packages.mcp-server` and `packages.ingest`
- `perSystem/processes.nix` — services-flake + process-compose-flake stack
- `scripts/schema.sql` — 8 tables: code_chunks, documents, github_{issues,issue_comments,prs,pr_comments}, sync_state, repo_index + BM25/HNSW indexes
- `scripts/ingest.py` — code ingest (tree-sitter symbols for TS/JS/Py, content_hash incremental, symbol_kind column)
- `scripts/ingest_docs.py` — markdown doc ingest (AGENTS.md, README, .agent/**)
- `scripts/ingest_github.py` — GitHub issues+PRs+comments (watermark incremental sync via sync_state)
- `scripts/mcp-server.py` — Python MCP server (kept as reference, replaced by Rust)
- `Cargo.toml` + `src/` — Rust binaries: `mcp-server` (6 tools) + `ingest` (code/docs/github)
- `justfile` — just index, index-docs, index-github, migrate, stats, sync-status

## MCP tools (Rust server)
1. `search_code` — hybrid+rerank, optional `language` + `symbol_kind` filters
2. `bm25_search` — BM25 only, same filters
3. `search_docs` — hybrid over documents table, optional `doc_kind` filter
4. `search_github` — hybrid over github_issues+prs, optional `entity_type`/`repo`/`state` filters
5. `list_repos` — list indexed repos with counts
6. `get_file` — retrieve all chunks for a file

## Project isolation (implemented)
- `project TEXT` column added to `code_chunks`, `documents`, `repo_index` (nullable, backward compat)
- Ingest: `--project <name>` flag on `code`, `docs`, `hackage`, `crate`, `pypi`, `git` subcommands
- MCP server: `PROJECTS=alpha,beta` env var → server-enforced whitelist; NULL-project chunks invisible when PROJECTS set
- `fetch_package` auto-tags with `self.projects.first()` (first project in PROJECTS list)
- GitHub tables NOT project-filtered (scoped by repo field already)
- `bm25_search` uses dynamic SQL for project filter (pg_search can't handle NULL-OR patterns)
- All other search functions use `$n::text[] IS NULL OR project = ANY($n::text[])` pattern
- Run `just migrate` to apply the new columns to an existing DB

## Known indexer gaps / fixes applied
- `MAX_CHUNKS_PER_FILE` was 128 → raised to 256. Files with many top-level declarations (e.g. serialise `Class.hs` with 140+ instances) were silently truncated.
- `collect_hs_decls` now recurses into `cpp` nodes so instances/functions inside `#if`/`#else` blocks are not silently dropped.
- When a symbol is missing from search despite the file being indexed, first check `MAX(end_line)` vs actual file length in the DB to detect truncation.

## Incremental sync pattern
- Code/docs: SHA-256 hash of file content stored in `content_hash`; skip if hash already in DB
- GitHub: `sync_state` table stores per-stream watermarks (ISO updated_at); `since=watermark` on issues/comments API; PR client-side filter
- `just migrate` runs schema.sql on existing DB (all CREATE IF NOT EXISTS + ALTER IF NOT EXISTS)

## Rust ingest binary (src/ingest/)
Separate binary in the same crate. Modules: main, embed, symbols, code, docs, github, hackage, crates, git, prune, repo_index.
- `ingest code <path> [--force]` — tree-sitter symbols (TS/JS/Py/Rust/Haskell) + line fallback; marks repo dirty in repo_index
- `ingest docs <path> [--force]` — markdown discovery + chunking
- `ingest github OWNER/REPO [--force] [--stream issues|prs|...]` — watermark sync
- `ingest hackage <pkg> <ver> [--force]` — fetch from CHaP/Hackage; registers clean in repo_index
- `ingest crate <pkg> <ver> [--force]` — fetch from crates.io; registers clean in repo_index
- `ingest pypi <pkg> <ver> [--force]` — fetch sdist from PyPI; repo_path="pypi::{pkg}-{ver}"; source_kind="pypi"
- `ingest git <url> [--rev|--branch|--tag] [--force] [--no-docs]` — shallow (branch/tag) or full (rev) clone; repo_path = git::<url>@<short_rev>
- `ingest list [--dirty] [--source-kind ...]` — show repo_index table
- `ingest prune dirty [--dry-run]` — delete all dirty repos
- `ingest prune old-versions [--package <name>] [--dry-run]` — keep only latest per package
- `ingest prune repo <repo_path> [--dry-run]` — delete specific repo
- Key deps: clap, ignore, sha2, hex, indicatif, chrono, tree-sitter (0.25) + grammar crates
- tree-sitter: `Language::from(LANG_CONST)` or `LANG_CONST.into()` to get Language
- Rust symbols: function_item, struct_item, enum_item, trait_item, type_item, const_item, impl_item methods (qualified as Type::method); walks impl body for functions
- Haskell symbols: collect HsDecl (kind, name, start/end rows) then group signature + consecutive same-name function equations into one symbol; includes Haddock comments
- `ingest_docs` signature: `(pool, repo_path, force, repo_path_override: Option<&str>)`
- lib.rs exposes ingest submodules (code, crates, docs, embed, hackage, repo_index, symbols) — any new module used by hackage/crates must be added here too
- justfile now uses `cargo run --release --bin ingest -- code|docs|github ...`

## Rust MCP server (src/)
Single-crate binary. Key rmcp patterns:
- struct needs `tool_router: ToolRouter<Self>` field, init: `Self::tool_router()`
- `#[tool_router]` on impl, `#[tool_handler]` on `impl ServerHandler for X`
- tool params: `Parameters<T>` where T: Deserialize + JsonSchema (via `use rmcp::schemars`)
- tool return type: `Result<CallToolResult, McpError>`, can be `async fn`
- start: `MyServer::new().serve(stdio()).await?.waiting().await?`
- features needed: `rmcp = { features = ["server", "transport-io", "macros"] }`
- Nix: `ORT_DYLIB_PATH = "${pkgs.onnxruntime}/lib/libonnxruntime.so"` in commonArgs + shellHook
- Bootstrap: `cargo generate-lockfile` → `git add Cargo.lock` → `nix flake update` → `nix build .#mcp-server`

## services-flake pattern (from pure-ledger)
```nix
process-compose.dev = {
  imports = [inputs.services-flake.processComposeModules.default];
  services.postgres."pg" = { enable = true; ... };
  services.ollama."llm" = { enable = true; ... };
  settings.processes = { /* custom */ };
};
```

## Key config choices
- PostgreSQL 17 + `extensions = ps: [ps.pg_search ps.pgvector]`
- `settings.shared_preload_libraries = "pg_search"` (required by pg_search)
- `settings.pg_search.enable_telemetry = false`
- `initialDatabases = [{name = "codebase"; schemas = [../scripts/schema.sql];}]`
- Ollama: `models = ["nomic-embed-text"]` (768-dim embeddings)
- dataDir defaults to `./data/${name}` (relative to CWD when running)

## Search strategy lessons (observed)
- `search_docs` only covers the `documents` table (markdown: `.md`, AGENTS.md, README, `.agent/**`). Never use it for `.tex` or other non-markdown content.
- `.tex` formal spec files land in `code_chunks` via `ingest code`. Use `search_code` or `bm25_search` for them.
- Not all subdirectories may be indexed. `eras/shelley/formal-spec/` was NOT in the index while `eras/shelley-ma/formal-spec/` was — gaps exist. If code search misses a known-important file, fall back to `Glob` + `Read` directly.
- `bm25_search` is best for exact symbol/keyword queries (e.g. `POOLREAP`, `PlReapState`). Semantic search over dense notation (LaTeX) is weak.
- For cardano-ledger formal specs, check `eras/*/formal-spec/epoch.tex` and `eras/*/formal-spec/delegation.tex` directly when search fails.

